{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self","id":1376437,"title":"Nimbus Tilt and self.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-24T14:52:41-07:00","id":1376437,"title":"Nimbus Tilt and self.","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Some questions about the Nimbus tilt: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can you affect yourself with the tilt? The core book says <i>&quot;If for whatever reason a character is aware of the effects, she can willingly submit to the Tilt regardless of her Resolve.&quot;</i> and that seems to cover yourself too.</li> <li>In Nameless and Accursed, a character Nimbus grants a bonus to Initiative, but the core book says that only Attributes or Skills can be affected, are there other stats that can be affected besides Attributes and Skills? If so, which ones?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T17:30:33-07:00","id":1376454,"title":"","content":"The Nimbus tilt does not affect the mage, otherwise they would be constantly benefiting from a buff or fighting off a debuff. A Weaving of Prime can be used to make it affect the caster.<br /> <br /> Initiative is Dex + Composure, so I would say applying it is reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:47:36-07:00","id":1376463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1376454#post1376454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nimbus tilt does not affect the mage, otherwise they would be constantly benefiting from a buff or fighting off a debuff. A Weaving of Prime can be used to make it affect the caster.<br /> <br /> Initiative is Dex + Composure, so I would say applying it is reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that not normally, but RAW could it be done? If you had only buffs it is doable.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T19:03:40-07:00","id":1376467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1376463#post1376463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but RAW could it be done?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be unreasonable for a custom Prime 3 spell to allow it, though. Maybe even Prime 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T09:25:28-07:00","id":1376721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self#post1376437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,[*]Can you affect yourself with the tilt? The core book says <i>&quot;If for whatever reason a character is aware of the effects, she can willingly submit to the Tilt regardless of her Resolve.&quot;</i> and that seems to cover yourself too.[/LIST]<br /> Thanks for the answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always ruled 'Yes' on this one? Its useful and lets people model a nimbus that makes them more intimidating/alluring/faster or so on. I kind of thought this was half the point of it actually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T11:37:07-07:00","id":1376734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1376721#post1376721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always ruled 'Yes' on this one? Its useful and lets people model a nimbus that makes them more intimidating/alluring/faster or so on. I kind of thought this was half the point of it actually?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to be alluring you want to be alluring to others, not yourself, same for intimidating. For a Nimbus like that you'd slap a negative modifier on the rolls of others to resist you. Mechanically, it's usually better to have a Nimbus that's a debuff than a buff, but some Mages are sweethearts whose symbolism aligns to improving others with no benefit to themselves (Except the results of their spells).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:09:13-07:00","id":1390181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1376721#post1376721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have always ruled 'Yes' on this one? Its useful and lets people model a nimbus that makes them more intimidating/alluring/faster or so on. I kind of thought this was half the point of it actually?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did that idea come from anyway? The source book never said you could do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:09:17-07:00","id":1390209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1390181#post1390181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where did that idea come from anyway? The source book never said you could do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say you can't either. It's a Tilt, you can use the mechanics to imitate pretty much whatever narrative effect you want within the guideline of those mechanics. If you had a Nimbus that gives a -2 to Composure or whatever it could be because you're overwhelmingly appealing in the moment when you flare it and it shakes their ability to hide their attraction or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:14:24-07:00","id":1402349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1390209#post1390209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't say you can't either. It's a Tilt, you can use the mechanics to imitate pretty much whatever narrative effect you want within the guideline of those mechanics. If you had a Nimbus that gives a -2 to Composure or whatever it could be because you're overwhelmingly appealing in the moment when you flare it and it shakes their ability to hide their attraction or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell are you talking about? Trace the conversation backwards. The mechanics show the tilt as something afflicted towards another. Going over the properties of the nimbi in both the corebook and signs of sorcery it is shown as a thing that changes the world to match your mystic identity, with no mention of it changing you. Sure you might lose your eye to match an Odin-like nimbus but that is a case of correlation as the shadow name may change your appearance and definitely your nimbus. Also, please don't shift the burden of proof or ask us to prove a negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T12:53:37-07:00","id":1402448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1402349#post1402349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell are you talking about? Trace the conversation backwards. The mechanics show the tilt as something afflicted towards another. Going over the properties of the nimbi in both the corebook and signs of sorcery it is shown as a thing that changes the world to match your mystic identity, with no mention of it changing you. Sure you might lose your eye to match an Odin-like nimbus but that is a case of correlation as the shadow name may change your appearance and definitely your nimbus. Also, please don't shift the burden of proof or ask us to prove a negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have completely missed the point, which was to illustrate that the mechanics can be used to support the narrative without rejiggering. In this particular instance we\u2019re talking about how a Nimbus Tilt could manifest as an aura of awesome projected from the Mage. Since the mechanics don\u2019t support the Nimbus affecting the Mage that generates it with a buff, how do we still make it work? Simple, we knock down the ability of those who are hit by the Nimbus to defend against the Mage\u2019s actions. The Mage projects an aura of awesome, everyone experiencing the Mage\u2019s Nimbus Tilt takes a penalty to treating the Mage as awesome, represented by a penalty to Composure rolls.<br /> <br /> Does that make it clearer for you? There\u2019s no need to be so defensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T16:02:42-07:00","id":1402490,"title":"","content":"Wow this topic sure has been inspiring! And I think what Mrmdubois is saying is that, you can use the Nimbus Tilt as designed in the book, but how you <i>describe</i> the effects in the narrative is something we can get creative with. Like if the Tilt inflicts the victim with a -2 to composure, we can <i>choose</i> to say that the Tilt manifests because they have a really scary nimbus that shakes the victim up, lowering their composure... OOOR, we can say that the Tilt is because the Mage is <i>ludicrously sexy</i>, so it makes the victim get butterflies in their stomach, and lowers their composure <i>that way.</i> So in both cases, the -2 is to composure, but <i>why</i> can be decided by the Mage's style, Path, and Shadow-Name. Perhaps the -2 to composure for an Obrimos is neither fear nor sexiness, but this overwhelming feeling of loss over the Fall, lowering composure and making the victim more susceptible to the Mage's teachings (or propaganda).<br /> <br /> I hope I got that right, if I did, this sounds cool. I hadn't thought of it like this before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T17:29:46-07:00","id":1402498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1402490#post1402490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow this topic sure has been inspiring! And I think what Mrmdubois is saying is that, you can use the Nimbus Tilt as designed in the book, but how you <i>describe</i> the effects in the narrative is something we can get creative with. Like if the Tilt inflicts the victim with a -2 to composure, we can <i>choose</i> to say that the Tilt manifests because they have a really scary nimbus that shakes the victim up, lowering their composure... OOOR, we can say that the Tilt is because the Mage is <i>ludicrously sexy</i>, so it makes the victim get butterflies in their stomach, and lowers their composure <i>that way.</i> So in both cases, the -2 is to composure, but <i>why</i> can be decided by the Mage's style, Path, and Shadow-Name. Perhaps the -2 to composure for an Obrimos is neither fear nor sexiness, but this overwhelming feeling of loss over the Fall, lowering composure and making the victim more susceptible to the Mage's teachings (or propaganda).<br /> <br /> I hope I got that right, if I did, this sounds cool. I hadn't thought of it like this before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T03:41:13-07:00","id":1402556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1402448#post1402448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to have completely missed the point, which was to illustrate that the mechanics can be used to support the narrative without rejiggering. In this particular instance we\u2019re talking about how a Nimbus Tilt could manifest as an aura of awesome projected from the Mage. Since the mechanics don\u2019t support the Nimbus affecting the Mage that generates it with a buff, how do we still make it work? Simple, we knock down the ability of those who are hit by the Nimbus to defend against the Mage\u2019s actions. The Mage projects an aura of awesome, everyone experiencing the Mage\u2019s Nimbus Tilt takes a penalty to treating the Mage as awesome, represented by a penalty to Composure rolls.<br /> <br /> Does that make it clearer for you? There\u2019s no need to be so defensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems we are no longer on the same topic anymore, pardon my frustrated confusion and forgetting that I am not supposed to cuss here. Please don't draw attention to my blunder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T07:22:47-07:00","id":1402594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1402556#post1402556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems we are no longer on the same topic anymore, pardon my frustrated confusion and forgetting that I am not supposed to cuss here. Please don't draw attention to my blunder.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the same topic. There's a mechanical difficulty, the Nimbus doesn't affect the Mage that produces it. I provided a work around that doesn't mess with the mechanics to get at least some of the desired effect. There is at least one drawback which I'm happy to point out, which is that a Mage won't be able to use their Nimbus in a vacuum to enhance themselves, which would be the case if a Mage could affect themselves with their own Nimbus Tilt. Still, as others have mentioned you can use Prime to get around that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T13:18:54-07:00","id":1402665,"title":"","content":"Letting the tilt effect the Mage is transitory *anyway* right? So its not that broken if people want it for mechanical &quot;cool factor&quot;, and honestly I avoid nimbus tilts cuz they make everything fiddly so I go light on their mechanics when they come up. So its probably a good &quot;table-to-table&quot; kinda thing to worry about, and again that custom prime spell solves everyones problem!<br /> <br /> As for lore and fluff? I'm guessing it is because it would be silly for a Mage's magical aura to &quot;overwhelm herself&quot; which is what the Tilt *is*?<br /> <br /> You could also homerule a merit that states the Mage focuses her identity inward so her Nimbus affects her but not other people? So if you wanna char whose gimmick is, say, nimbus manifests as anonymous ancestors who support him, and &quot;Tilts&quot; himself doing it...<br /> <br /> <br /> But for me the mechanics of the Tilt are too complicated and too transitort and chaotic too fret too much about, but the numbers can be used as a measuring stick for &quot;how much acting&quot; you can expect from someone influenced by it? Like if some Moros whose Tilt is -2 Stamina by making people feel their impending death, sure you can kill them easier or something mechanical, but what about intimidation? An NPC who just lost all their vigor might be Beaten Down just from the Tilt x3 So we can use em for story opportunities!!<br /> <br /> Put short, Nimbus are cool and flashy but the core mechanic of the game lies elsewhere so, do what fits your table but don't get hung up on something minor??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T21:34:17-07:00","id":1402735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376437-nimbus-tilt-and-self?p=1402594#post1402594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is the same topic. There's a mechanical difficulty, the Nimbus doesn't affect the Mage that produces it. I provided a work around that doesn't mess with the mechanics to get at least some of the desired effect. There is at least one drawback which I'm happy to point out, which is that a Mage won't be able to use their Nimbus in a vacuum to enhance themselves, which would be the case if a Mage could affect themselves with their own Nimbus Tilt. Still, as others have mentioned you can use Prime to get around that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I meant, we were not on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}